{
  "title": "Δ-Complex Cohomology Visualiser",
  "schema": "delta-cohomology",
  "version": 1,
  "url": "https://teoyujie.org/visuals/delta-cohomology/",
  "scope": "Simplicial cohomology of S², T² and RP² from Δ-complexes with two 2-simplices U and L each, over ℤ, 𝔽₂ and 𝔽₃: boundary matrices derived from face maps and gluing, coboundaries as transposes, kernels and images, Smith normal form, and cup products by Alexander–Whitney.",
  "conventions": [
    "A 2-simplex [p0, p1, p2] has boundary Σ (−1)^i d_i, where d_i deletes vertex i; an edge [p, q] has boundary q − p.",
    "Each face is compared with the edge it is glued to: +1 when the face's vertex order runs along the edge's arrow, −1 against it. A flipped simplex negates its generator.",
    "Rows of ∂₂ are edges a, b, c and its columns are U, L; rows of ∂₁ are vertices and its columns are edges. δᵏ = ∂ₖ₊₁ᵀ.",
    "Hᵏ = ker δᵏ / im δᵏ⁻¹ is computed with the Smith normal form over ℤ and row reduction over 𝔽ₚ, never from ranks alone.",
    "Cup products use the Alexander–Whitney front and back faces (φ⌣ψ)[p0,p1,p2] = φ[p0,p1]·ψ[p1,p2]."
  ],
